WEBVTT

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.940
<i></i><b>The Empire</b>

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.940
<i></i><b>The Empire</b>

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:39.390
Hup...

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.760
There we go. Done for the day.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:44.580
Thanks for your help, Jack.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:49.420
Here's your pay, and you can have this, too.

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:53.350
Thanks a lot, boss!

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:54.920
Want a ride on the cart?

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.930
Nah, that's okay. I'll run back.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.190
You sure are strong.

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:03.430
It is just about time for 
you to leave, isn't it?

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.330
Yeah. See ya!

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:09.200
I'll be calling you again!

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.940
Sorry I'm late, guys!

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.700
Hey, Jack. Good to see you.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:22.200
If you'd been any later, 
we would've left without you.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.930
Whew, good thing I got here when I did!

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.560
Where'd you get that?

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:28.960
The farmer gave it to me for helping out.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.760
Wow, that's a lot.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.210
You're taking them with you?

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:37.140
I thought I'd give them 
to the master at Nekoya.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:38.970
Good idea.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:43.220
Oh, yeah! Did you guys bring your money?

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.360
Of course.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:45.470
Yep.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.330
All right, then, let's go!

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:52.110
I can't wait.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.460
Okay, ready. Let it down.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.000
Got it!

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.570
Okay, Kento, you're next.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:19.310
Better be careful. You're slow as it is.

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:21.480
Whoa! Don't do that!

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:24.560
I know I fell once before, but come on!

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.510
Yeah, okay, sorry.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:33.770
You okay?!

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.350
Ow, ow, ow...

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:37.820
I'm okay!

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:38.520
Here.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.900
Okay, let's open it.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:51.250
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:47.840
Yeah.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.190
Welcome!

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:55.930
Take a seat wherever you'd like.

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:00.690
Hey, Miss Aletta.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:03.700
Hi there. Give me just a minute, okay?

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:04.510
Sure.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.260
Here are your complimentary 
glasses of water and wet hand towels.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:15.440
I still can't get used to that.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:16.270
Yeah...

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:22.030
Is she using some kind of magic 
to speak directly into our minds?

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.640
I've never heard of any magic like that.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.030
We didn't get to order.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:28.520
Excuse me.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:30.290
I'll be right there!

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:32.790
What can I get for you?

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.350
The hamburger meal!

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.290
With cola to drink!

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.300
Okay, coming right up!

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:45.300
Oh, also, could you give 
these oranie to the master?

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:48.950
Will do.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:49.960
Thanks!

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.940
We got an order for three hamburger meals.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.060
Cola with all three of them.

00:04:57.590 --> 00:05:01.320
Got it. Could you get the drinks ready?

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.410
Sure.

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:06.070
Also, Jack said to give these to you.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.080
So many of them...

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.720
These are nice onions.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.580
I'm so excited for this hamburger.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:21.590
I know! It's nothing like 
the food we usually eat!

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:25.040
Yeah. And just nine copper coins 
for such a delicious meal.

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.090
It's unbelievably cheap.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.630
Uh-huh!

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:31.300
Still, though...

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:39.350
This restaurant sure gets 
a lot of demihumans.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:41.390
I wonder where they come from.

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:42.780
No idea.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:45.620
But it just means there are many types

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:49.760
of demihumans living in our world that we 
can only see in this restaurant, right?

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:52.790
Right!

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:55.360
E-Excuse me...

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.440
J-Jack!

00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.790
H-Hey!

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:02.560
Tell me, what sort of place do you live in?

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:08.550
Omelette rice. Delicious.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:12.120
Wow, so that stuff's called "omelette rice"?

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:14.160
It really does look good!

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:17.330
Wait, I mean... uh...

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:22.650
You... where... from?

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:25.820
Omelette rice not for you.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:28.500
No, I'm not gonna take it.

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:44.130
Warrior buy here.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:46.640
Buy and take home.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:50.840
Forest village, omelette, tradition.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.880
Oh, I get it!

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:54.350
Huh? What'd he say?

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:57.900
There's a village of lizardmen in the forest,

00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:59.980
and he lives there as a warrior.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.660
Wow...

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:04.230
Jack, you're amazing.

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:07.320
We live in huts in the mountains.

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:11.240
Mountain huts? Don't you get cold at night?

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:14.660
Booze keeps us warm!

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.470
And we've got bonfires, too.

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.250
We don't get cold.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.250
Wow...

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:23.050
How old are you boys?

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:24.340
I'm fourteen.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:26.180
Same.

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:28.840
I'm fifteen, a year older than them.

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:33.160
I see. Too young for booze, then.

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:35.840
All of the booze here is great.

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:38.280
Try them out when you're all grown up.

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:47.800
That looks awesome!

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.280
You look like you're having fun.

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:51.950
Hey, Master!

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.340
Thank you for waiting.

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:59.540
<i>Hamburger</i>

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:58.900
Here are your hamburger meals.

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:02.040
Yes! It's here!

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.890
Kento, you're drooling.

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:08.550
Huh?! No way!

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:11.760
Thanks for the oni—the oranie.

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:14.430
I gave you all extra fries.

00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:18.560
Well, then, enjoy.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.310
All right, let's dig in!

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:23.210
Yeah!

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.570
So good!

00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:33.670
The little specks on the surface

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:37.780
are a great textural contrast 
with the soft bread!

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:40.230
The marmett is both sweet and sour,

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:42.590
the oranie is so sweet,

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:45.130
the lelesa is so crunchy,

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:47.790
and the kauri is perfectly pickled!

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.800
This is delicious!

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:55.620
The soft sourness of the white sauce, 
the yellow sauce, and the sour red sauce

00:08:55.620 --> 00:09:00.760
work with the gooey melted cheese to bring 
out the flavor of the meat in the middle.

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:06.810
<i>A hamburger is all about eating meat!</i>

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:08.260
<i>Maybe because it was ground so finely</i>

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:09.610
<i>before being pressed together to cook,</i>

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:12.480
<i>it's so tender, I can 
bite right through it!</i>

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:17.000
<i>As I chew it up, all the savory 
flavor bursts right out</i>

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:19.320
<i>and fills my whole mouth!</i>

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:22.220
<i>Even stuck between all the 
vegetables and cheese,</i>

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:25.360
<i>the meat has a powerful enough presence 
to break through them all!</i>

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:29.610
This is the best!

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:35.160
Mm, this is good!

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:38.470
I wonder how they make cola, anyway.

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:41.680
It'd be awesome if we could 
drink this every day.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:45.600
I heard there's a spring near 
the volcano that gets bubbly.

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:49.470
Maybe they use the water from there?

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:52.730
Wow... Well, that's a 
future sorcerer for you.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:58.070
Mm, that's good!

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:01.510
It's crispy on the outside 
and hot and fluffy on the inside!

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:06.780
No one in our world would believe that 
just a little salt makes these so good.

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:15.530
They're plenty good on their own,

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:17.880
but they're good with this red sauce, too.

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:22.580
I wonder how they prepare these 
to get them this way, though.

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:25.050
It's nothing like what we have at home.

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:28.140
They must cook them in the finest oil.

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:32.810
I bet they're really careful about 
the frying time and temperature, too.

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:47.230
We could still eat more, huh?

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:48.190
Of course!

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:49.140
Yeah.

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:50.120
We'd like to order!

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:51.750
Certainly.

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:54.610
Seconds on the hamburger 
meal for all three of us!

00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:56.510
With cola to drink!

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:59.210
Your order has been accepted.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:05.440
Anyway, we have to set off 
on our journey pretty soon.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:07.390
Where should we go first?

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:11.270
Let's see... I'd like to 
go to the imperial capital.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.520
The volcano would be awesome,

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:18.020
but I want to check out the Land of Sand,
 where magic is so advanced.

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:19.020
You, Jack?

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:20.900
I want...

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:24.030
to go to all the places 
I've never been to before!

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:28.180
Sounds good.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:29.060
Oh!

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:30.040
What is it?

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:33.040
Does this mean we won't be 
able to come here anymore?

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:37.550
Don't worry, Jack. Just look around you.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:40.980
Those doors must be all over the world.

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:42.920
You're right!

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:46.560
It might be fun to look for 
other doors leading here.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:48.580
That sounds like a blast!

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:52.940
Here are your hamburger meals.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:54.190
Thanks!

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:03.090
<b>Western Restaurant Nekoya</b>

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:02.290
So good!

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:10.000
Okay, we ate what we wanted 
to eat. Ready to head back?

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:12.750
Yeah. I still need to train more.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:15.970
Yeah. The day we leave is getting closer.

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.960
Thank you very much.

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:27.260
Thank you very much!

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:33.540
Things have finally settled down.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:36.270
Want to eat your meals now, while there's time?

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:37.930
Sure!

00:12:37.930 --> 00:12:38.740
Yes.

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:40.780
Welcome!

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:41.980
Can I take your order?

00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:43.240
Curry rice.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.110
C-Coming right up!

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:46.280
Welcome.

00:12:46.550 --> 00:12:51.170
Alphonse-san, I could make 
your usual curry rice for you,

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:53.290
but I wanted to consult with you first.

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:55.790
About what? Let's hear it.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:58.450
In addition to curry rice and chicken curry,

00:12:58.450 --> 00:13:01.920
I'm thinking about serving 
a third type of curry.

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:05.180
Oh? That's something to look forward to.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:09.490
So I was hoping you'd be willing 
to taste-test a few types for me.

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:12.930
What?! Of course I will assist you!

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:15.440
Thank you.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:16.780
Curry...

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:24.690
I'm sorry. I was just about 
to prepare my employees' meals.

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:30.200
Were you? Then why not have them 
taste-test your new flavors, too?

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:35.960
I'd like to hear this little lady's 
opinion as a fellow curry lover.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.890
I see. Then if you'll excuse me...

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:46.260
And what do you say, young demon?

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:49.340
Master, more opinions would 
benefit you, would they not?

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:52.820
All right. I'll take you up on that.

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:04.450
We haven't shared a table like 
this since the day we first met.

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:10.530
I never would have imagined a little 
lady like you could eat that much.

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:13.110
Thank you for paying for my meal back then.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.850
Please. It was nothing.

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:17.040
Thank you for waiting.

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:19.840
Ah, three different types!

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:22.060
This green one is curry, too?

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:24.630
Yes. That one is green curry.

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:24.880
<i>Green Curry</i>

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:28.590
<i>Beef Tendon Curry</i>

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:27.050
The dark-colored one is beef tendon curry,

00:14:27.710 --> 00:14:30.420
and the last one is soup curry.

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:31.930
<i>Soup Curry</i>

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:33.930
They smell good.

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:34.990
Indeed.

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:39.630
All right, shall we start with 
this so-called green curry?

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:43.800
Thank you, god of demons, 
for this, my daily bread.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:45.190
I shall now partake.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:46.440
As will I.

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:50.120
<i>The color is so different from chicken curry.</i>

00:14:57.340 --> 00:15:00.730
<i>The refreshing aroma and 
invigorating spiciness...</i>

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:06.190
<i>And the mellow, milk-like sweetness 
that surrounds the heat</i>

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:08.030
<i>stimulates the appetite.</i>

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:16.630
Ah, this is indeed curry, too.

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:19.460
I could get hooked on this unique fragrance.

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:21.480
Yes... It's good!

00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:27.230
It has such a sweet, mellow—

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:29.240
Wait, no! That's hot!

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:37.900
It was so sweet and mellow 
when it first hit my tongue...

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:39.750
It really fooled me.

00:15:40.070 --> 00:15:43.120
Sorry about that. I should've 
warned you first.

00:15:43.530 --> 00:15:46.630
That's all right! 
It's spicy, but it's delicious!

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:57.390
It goes so well with rice! 
And bread, too, I bet!

00:15:57.390 --> 00:16:00.740
Yeah. Bread isn't normally served with this,

00:16:00.740 --> 00:16:03.320
but there's something called 
"naan" that's similar to bread.

00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:05.400
You dip it in the curry and eat it.

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:08.320
It's made with the same flour as our bread,

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:10.660
but it's cooked by sticking the 
dough to the inside of the oven,

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:11.710
making it more savory.

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:13.100
Naan?

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.340
I can't wait to try it!

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:27.590
Next is...

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:33.710
All right!

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:38.820
It's much more watery than curry rice.

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:46.100
But it's much more flavorful than 
its appearance would suggest!

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:54.110
Mm! It's good!

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:58.740
<i>The roux, prepared in 
the form of smooth soup,</i>

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:03.250
<i>carries the distinct flavors 
of the vegetables and spices.</i>

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:07.920
<i>The cobbler's tubers, karoots, 
and eggs all make their presence known.</i>

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:11.710
<i>The fragrance of the herbs gives a 
stronger impression than the spiciness.</i>

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:21.470
Dipping rice in the soup makes it 
go down as smoothly as a drink.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:24.700
Soup curry... A drink?

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:36.320
That was delicious!

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.330
This is the last one.

00:17:42.130 --> 00:17:46.330
It looks like the curry rice 
that Alphonse-san always eats,

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:48.470
but the color is much darker.

00:17:48.470 --> 00:17:50.590
Yes, that it is.

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:54.450
It smells very nice.

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:58.590
Delicious...

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:07.550
<i>The vegetables meld together with the roux,</i>

00:18:07.550 --> 00:18:09.320
<i>just like in chicken curry.</i>

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:14.860
<i>But the strong savoriness of the 
meat gives it a complex flavor.</i>

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:19.810
I made the beef tendon curry with more 
emphasis on richness than regular curry.

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:21.570
Oh, I see!

00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:23.840
The meat in it is beef tendon.

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:27.580
The longer you cook it, 
the more tender and savory it gets.

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:35.350
Wow! The meat just melted away in my mouth!

00:18:35.350 --> 00:18:37.890
I've never had meat like this before!

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:42.850
Mm! Delicious!

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:53.780
<i>Meat that melts in your mouth?</i>

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:58.110
<i>It melted away right on the top of my tongue!</i>

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:01.360
<i>It's not at all like the 
meat in chicken curry.</i>

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:04.370
<i>My teeth cut right through it instantly,</i>

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:06.680
<i>and when it hits my tongue, it dissolves.</i>

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:11.500
<i>And the sweetness of the fat in the 
meat enhances the curry's flavor.</i>

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:25.680
Delicious.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:27.980
Delicious!

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:29.880
So good!

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:44.430
What do you think? Was there 
one you particularly liked?

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:48.000
Hmm... All of them were good, but...

00:19:49.090 --> 00:19:52.590
I think we'd all say the 
beef tendon curry, right?

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:55.880
Oh, well... actually...

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:59.590
Of these three, perhaps. But...

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:05.180
I like my usual chicken curry the best.

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:05.180
I like my usual curry rice the best.

00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:17.800
All this talk is making 
me want some curry rice.

00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:20.310
Master, one plate of curry rice!

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:22.650
What would you girls like?

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:24.670
I want chicken curry.

00:20:24.670 --> 00:20:27.410
I-I'd like more beef tendon curry!

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:31.360
Then add a chicken curry and a 
beef tendon curry to that order.

00:20:31.360 --> 00:20:32.540
Coming right up.

00:20:37.610 --> 00:20:39.380
<i>This really is the best!</i>

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:44.610
<i>The pairing of spicy curry and 
sweet pork just can't be beat!</i>

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:52.640
Curry rice reigns supreme!

00:20:56.720 --> 00:20:59.150
Chicken curry is delicious.

00:21:00.290 --> 00:21:03.000
So you still like your 
usual curry the most, huh?

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:03.900
Yes.

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:05.680
I suppose so.

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:08.470
Still, I'm impressed to learn that

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:11.660
there can be so many different 
types of the same dish.

00:21:12.090 --> 00:21:13.810
Are there any others?

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:16.670
Master! Does the world you come from

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:20.770
have other types of curry 
besides the ones we had today?

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:21.670
Yes.

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:25.050
There's seafood curry, 
which is made with seafood...

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:29.260
Palak paneer, which is made 
with spinach and cheese...

00:21:29.940 --> 00:21:32.590
Dal tadka, which is made with lentils...

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:35.690
And many, many others.

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:38.600
Wow, I had no idea!

00:21:38.970 --> 00:21:41.940
I bet they're all delicious!

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:44.940
I want to try those types 
of curry someday, too.

00:21:46.140 --> 00:21:48.950
One of them might even be better than these.

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:51.410
I might make them one day.

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:54.140
If I do, I'll ask you to 
taste-test for me again.

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:55.960
I'd appreciate that!

00:21:56.600 --> 00:22:00.650
It seems there are still many 
more types of curry that

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:03.340
I've yet to discover in the other world.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:42.350
<i>Children's Lunch</i>

00:23:42.350 --> 00:23:50.250
<i>Cream Croquette</i>
